WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.080
I was at the Startup Venezuela Summit,

2
00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:05.870
at Caracas Campus, and honestly,

3
00:00:05.870 --> 00:00:08.910
I had never been to an event like it.

4
00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:12.680
There were talks all day, people from other countries

5
00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:16.930
making connections, and everyone was building every kind

6
00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:18.910
of product you can imagine.

7
00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:23.200
We heard Víctor Cárdenas of Slash again,

8
00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:28.260
and Pedro Vallenilla of Cashea.

9
00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:34.510
We were also at a workshop with Enrique Rivas of Fina

10
00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:37.250
and the team of Innoven.

11
00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:43.850
I applied with Salvalo at Innoven's stand and stuck out

12
00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:48.300
our photo on the wall of Venezuelan founders to leave

13
00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:49.280
our mark.

14
00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:56.080
I also met a lot of people like one of the co-founders

15
00:00:56.080 --> 00:00:57.100
of Rial.

16
00:00:57.100 --> 00:01:03.000
What I took out most from those two days is that

17
00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:09.310
building a startup is hard, but it's worth it.

18
00:01:09.310 --> 00:01:13.510
With ambition, drive, and passion,

19
00:01:13.510 --> 00:01:14.580
you can make it.

20
00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:18.120
It doesn't matter your age, your country,

21
00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:19.780
or where you come from.

22
00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:20.780
If you're willing to do it, it's worth it.

23
00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:25.760
If you're willing to do it, it can be done.

24
00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:30.120
And the other thing is what Steve Jobs said,

25
00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:36.400
that the people crazy enough to think they can change

26
00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:40.340
the world are the ones who actually do it.

27
00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:43.030
I got home super excited.

28
00:01:43.030 --> 00:01:48.910
Still processing all the talks and everything I lived in

29
00:01:48.910 --> 00:01:50.938
those two days.
